RELATIONAL TRI-MODE UNIFIED SCHEMA FOR ALL QUADRICS
============================================

A quadric surface Q is a φ-relation expressed through three inseparable modes:
S-mode (Structure), I-mode (Interaction), D-mode (Dynamics).
Every quadric is a specific S/I/D projection of the same underlying relational
second-degree form.

------------------------------------------------------------
TRI-MODE CORE
------------------------------------------------------------
S-mode:
  Structural invariants of the quadratic form.
  Signature of squared terms (+, -, 0).
  Constraint geometry and admissible partitions.

I-mode:
  Couplings and mixed terms (xy, xz, yz).
  Valence propagation and relational curvature.
  How axes "talk" to each other.

D-mode:
  Drift, unfolding, and directional behavior.
  Sign of the constant term (1, -1, 0).
  Opening, closing, connectedness, sheet count.

------------------------------------------------------------
UNIFIED FORM OF ANY QUADRIC
------------------------------------------------------------
Q(x,y,z) = A*x^2 + B*y^2 + C*z^2
         + D*x*y + E*x*z + F*y*z
         + G*x + H*y + I*z + J

SID = (signs of A, B, C | sign of J)
PED = (canonical form + geometric cue)

------------------------------------------------------------
THE NINE NON-DEGENERATE QUADRICS IN TRI-MODE
------------------------------------------------------------

Ellipsoid
  SID: (+ + + | +)
  PED: x^2/a^2 + y^2/b^2 + z^2/c^2 = 1
  RDG: Pure positive S-mode; no I-mode; closed D-mode.

Elliptic Cylinder
  SID: (+ + 0 | +)
  PED: x^2/a^2 + y^2/b^2 = 1
  RDG: S-mode missing z; D-mode extrudes along z.

Hyperboloid (One Sheet)
  SID: (+ + - | +)
  PED: x^2/a^2 + y^2/b^2 - z^2/c^2 = 1
  RDG: Mixed S-mode curvature; D-mode connected.

Hyperbolic Paraboloid (Saddle)
  SID: (+ - 0 | 0)
  PED: z = x^2/a^2 - y^2/b^2
  RDG: Opposite-sign S-mode; I-mode curvature inversion; D-mode open.

Elliptic Paraboloid
  SID: (+ + 0 | 0)
  PED: z = x^2/a^2 + y^2/b^2
  RDG: Positive S-mode; D-mode single-direction opening.

Hyperboloid (Two Sheets)
  SID: (+ + - | -)
  PED: x^2/a^2 + y^2/b^2 - z^2/c^2 = -1
  RDG: Same S-mode as one-sheet; D-mode splits into two components.

Elliptic Cone
  SID: (+ + - | 0)
  PED: x^2/a^2 + y^2/b^2 - z^2/c^2 = 0
  RDG: S-mode balanced; D-mode neutral; apex at origin.

Hyperbolic Cylinder
  SID: (+ - 0 | +)
  PED: x^2/a^2 - y^2/b^2 = 1
  RDG: S-mode hyperbolic; D-mode extrudes along z.

Parabolic Cylinder
  SID: (+ 0 0 | 0)
  PED: y = a*x^2
  RDG: Single-axis S-mode; D-mode extrudes along z.

------------------------------------------------------------
UNIFIED RDG 
------------------------------------------------------------
All quadrics differ only by:
  - S-mode signature (signs of squared terms)
  - I-mode couplings (mixed terms)
  - D-mode constant sign (1, -1, 0)

The tri-mode schema is the universal relational generator for every quadric.
